1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,900
Two spoonfuls of peanut butter a day,
that's all it takes to change at

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:06,210
least four things in your body after 60.

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:10,640
Three of them are good news, one of them
isn't, and almost nobody talks

4
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:15,880
about it. Today, we'll go through all four,
with real studies, not miracle

5
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:20,600
promises. You'll also learn how much to
eat, how to choose a good jar in

6
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:24,700
10 seconds, and the truth about that popular
claim that peanut butter before

7
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:30,180
bed melts belly fat. Quick note, this video
is general education, not medical

8
00:00:30,180 --> 00:00:32,810
advice. All sources are in
the description.

9
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:37,640
If you have kidney disease, a peanut
allergy, or take medication, talk

10
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:38,910
to your doctor first.

11
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:42,170
Let's start with what's
actually in a serving.

12
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:48,040
Two tablespoons of smooth peanut butter,
about 32 grams, have roughly 190

13
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:53,980
calories. About 7 grams of protein, 16
grams of fat, and around 2 grams

14
00:00:53,980 --> 00:00:59,000
of fiber. Most of that fat is the
unsaturated kind, similar to what you

15
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,890
find in nuts and olive oil.

16
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:05,190
And peanuts also bring potassium,
magnesium, and vitamin E.

17
00:01:05,540 --> 00:01:09,630
In other words, it's a small spoon
with a lot packed inside.

18
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:13,390
And that's exactly why it can help
you, or work against you.

19
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:17,150
The first change, your muscles get
more building blocks.

20
00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:22,460
7 grams of protein may not sound like much,
but after 60, the body needs

21
00:01:22,460 --> 00:01:24,730
more protein than before, not less.

22
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,290
At least 1.0 to 1.2 grams per
kilo every day.

23
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:33,820
On its own, peanut butter won't get you to
the 25 to 30 grams per meal

24
00:01:33,820 --> 00:01:35,850
that muscles respond to best.

25
00:01:36,320 --> 00:01:37,950
But it's a great team player.

26
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:42,360
Put two spoonfuls on whole grain toast and
drink a glass of milk, and you're

27
00:01:42,360 --> 00:01:44,950
already close to 20 grams of
protein at breakfast.

28
00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:48,030
And remember, muscles need movement too.

29
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:49,720
Protein gives them the materials.

30
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:54,520
Walking, climbing stairs, and standing up
from a chair tell them to use

31
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:58,810
those materials. The second change
surprised researchers.

32
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:03,480
In a study at Purdue University, women at
high risk of type 2 diabetes

33
00:02:03,480 --> 00:02:08,320
ate the same breakfast on different days,
sometimes with about 3 tablespoons

34
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:10,930
of peanut butter, sometimes without.

35
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:14,960
When they had peanut butter at breakfast,
they reported less desire to

36
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:16,320
eat in the hours that followed.

37
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:21,570
And their blood sugar rose less after
lunch, a meal they ate hours later.

38
00:02:21,780 --> 00:02:25,950
To be honest, it was a small
study, with only 15 women.

39
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:27,950
But it fits what many people notice.

40
00:02:28,340 --> 00:02:32,340
A breakfast with protein and fat keeps you
satisfied much longer than toast

41
00:02:32,340 --> 00:02:36,680
and jam alone. And when you're less
hungry, it's easier not to snack on

42
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:37,990
cookies before lunch.

43
00:02:38,580 --> 00:02:40,520
The third change is about the long term.

44
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:45,740
In the nurses' health study, researchers
followed almost 84,000 women for

45
00:02:45,740 --> 00:02:50,460
16 years. Those who ate peanut butter five
or more times a week had about

46
00:02:50,460 --> 00:02:55,520
a 21% lower risk of developing type 2
diabetes than those who almost never

47
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:59,540
ate it. Another large study followed
people in the United States and in

48
00:02:59,540 --> 00:03:03,800
Shanghai, China. In the American group,
those who ate the most peanuts

49
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:08,420
had a 21% lower risk of dying during the
study period, especially from

50
00:03:08,420 --> 00:03:11,710
heart disease. Now these are
observational studies.

51
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:13,910
They show a link, not proof.

52
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:18,040
People who eat peanuts may have other
healthy habits too, but the results

53
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:22,000
point in the same direction across very
different groups of people, and

54
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,590
that's worth paying attention to.

55
00:03:24,060 --> 00:03:26,790
A question many people over 60 ask.

56
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:28,970
Is peanut butter bad for cholesterol?

57
00:03:29,340 --> 00:03:31,670
Here's something that surprises
a lot of people.

58
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:35,640
Peanut butter has no cholesterol at all
because it comes from a plant.

59
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:39,330
Cholesterol in food only comes
from animal products.

60
00:03:39,620 --> 00:03:41,590
What matters more is the type of fat.

61
00:03:41,940 --> 00:03:44,570
Peanut butter is mostly unsaturated fat.

62
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:49,540
Health organizations recommend replacing
saturated fats, like butter, with

63
00:03:49,540 --> 00:03:54,010
unsaturated ones to help keep
cholesterol in a healthier range.

64
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:58,160
So spreading peanut butter on your toast
instead of butter is generally

65
00:03:58,160 --> 00:04:03,210
a smart swap. Just keep the portion small
because the calories are similar.

66
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:07,450
And now the fourth change, the one
almost nobody mentions.

67
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:11,110
If you're not careful, peanut butter
can make you gain weight.

68
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:14,010
It's one of the most calorie dense
foods in your kitchen.

69
00:04:14,340 --> 00:04:19,170
Two spoonfuls are about 190 calories, but a
lot of people don't measure.

70
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:23,340
They dip the spoon straight into the jar a
few times, and four heaping

71
00:04:23,340 --> 00:04:28,250
spoons can easily pass 380 calories,
almost like a small meal.

72
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:30,320
So does peanut butter make you fat?

73
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:33,710
Only if you add it on top of
everything you already eat.

74
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:37,970
The researchers from the Diabetes Study
made exactly this recommendation.

75
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:42,760
Use nuts to replace less healthy foods,
like refined bread or processed

76
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:45,150
meats, not in addition to them.

77
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:47,970
Here's the 10 second test at
the supermarket.

78
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:50,550
Turn the jar around and read
the ingredients.

79
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:53,850
The best list is short peanuts
and maybe salt.

80
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:57,940
Many popular brands add sugar and
hydrogenated or palm oils to make it

81
00:04:57,940 --> 00:04:59,000
sweeter and creamier.

82
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:03,480
You don't need that. And if you watch your
blood pressure, look for a version

83
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:05,970
with no added salt. One more tip.

84
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:09,410
Natural peanut butter often has a
layer of oil on top.

85
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:13,680
That's normal. Just stir it well and keep
the jar in the refrigerator after

86
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:16,070
opening if you want it to separate less.

87
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:21,100
If you can't find a jar with just peanuts
or you want to save money, you

88
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:22,650
can make peanut butter at home.

89
00:05:22,980 --> 00:05:27,580
All you need is roasted peanuts without
skins and a food processor or a

90
00:05:27,580 --> 00:05:30,710
strong blender. Blend for about
5 to 10 minutes.

91
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:36,380
First it turns into crumbs, then a thick
paste and then, suddenly, it becomes

92
00:05:36,380 --> 00:05:39,990
creamy. Stop every couple of
minutes to scrape the sides.

93
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:42,590
Add a pinch of salt if you
like and that's it.

94
00:05:42,840 --> 00:05:46,440
Store it in a clean glass jar in the
refrigerator and it keeps for a few

95
00:05:46,440 --> 00:05:50,990
weeks. No sugar, no added oils, and you
know exactly what's inside.

96
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:55,560
For most people, 1 to 2 tablespoons a
day is a sensible amount.

97
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:59,700
Use a real measuring spoon for a week just
to see what a portion looks

98
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:03,190
like. If you're trying to lose
weight, 1 spoon is enough.

99
00:06:03,420 --> 00:06:06,700
But if you're losing weight without wanting
to, which is common in older

100
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:11,420
age, 2 spoons a day is one of the easiest
ways to add good calories and

101
00:06:11,420 --> 00:06:14,870
protein. In that case, talk to
your doctor too.

102
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:19,070
Some easy ways to eat it on whole grain
toast with banana slices.

103
00:06:19,340 --> 00:06:24,400
Stir it into warm oatmeal as a dip for
apple slices or blend it into a

104
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:28,230
smoothie with milk and a banana, which is
great if chewing is difficult.

105
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:32,540
You can even mix a spoon with a little
warm water, lemon and garlic to

106
00:06:32,540 --> 00:06:34,810
make a quick sauce for
vegetables or chicken.

107
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:39,380
Now, about those videos promising that 1
spoon of peanut butter before

108
00:06:39,380 --> 00:06:42,290
bed melts belly fat like a
weight loss drug.

109
00:06:42,540 --> 00:06:46,250
I looked for the evidence and no food
melts belly fat on its own.

110
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:47,430
Peanut butter included.

111
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:51,860
If you get hungry at night, a small portion
of peanut butter on toast is

112
00:06:51,860 --> 00:06:56,210
a much better choice than sweets because the
protein and fat keep you satisfied.

113
00:06:56,660 --> 00:06:59,590
Just count it as part of your day,
not as a magic trick.

114
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:02,010
Now, the honest part.

115
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:06,440
If you have kidney disease, peanuts
contain potassium and phosphorus, 2

116
00:07:06,440 --> 00:07:07,890
minerals you may need to limit.

117
00:07:08,180 --> 00:07:11,050
Ask your doctor or dietitian how
much is safe for you.

118
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:14,890
If you have trouble swallowing, thick peanut
butter can stick in the throat.

119
00:07:15,200 --> 00:07:19,680
Spread it thin, mix it into oatmeal or
smoothies and always have something

120
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:24,240
to drink with it. And of course, if you're
allergic to peanuts, stay away

121
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:28,330
completely. A peanut allergy can
be serious at any age.

122
00:07:28,900 --> 00:07:32,910
So, what really happens when you eat
peanut butter every day after 60?

123
00:07:33,220 --> 00:07:35,750
1. Your muscles get extra protein.

124
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:40,680
2. You stay full longer and your blood
sugar may rise less after the next

125
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:46,030
meal. 3. Large studies link it to lower
diabetes risk and longer life.

126
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:49,760
And 4. If you don't measure, it can
make you gain weight.

127
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:55,840
1 to 2 measured spoonfuls from a jar with
just peanuts replacing something

128
00:07:55,840 --> 00:07:59,030
less healthy. That's the
smart way to do it.

129
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:00,510
Do you eat peanut butter?

130
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:02,050
How do you like it best?

131
00:08:02,500 --> 00:08:03,630
Tell me in the comments.

132
00:08:04,140 --> 00:08:08,150
And if you want more cheap foods that help
protect your legs after 60,

133
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:09,950
watch this video next.

134
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:11,130
See you there.
